      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I read the description and I thought \"works on my machine\". I then read the reproduction steps and I thought \"this is not a bug\".\n\nThat's on you, if you allow a person to bypass your safety shield settings with \"Show Avatar\" forced on them. You clicked on it.\n\nI personally disagree that this should be changed at all, I may want to see one person temporarily use a globally blocked avatar or only that one person, without adjusting my globally blocked avatars for everyone.\n\nIf you feel strongly otherwise about this, maybe make a new [feature request](https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests) topic to change the behavior?",
